## Instructions

1. **Replace the title** with your diagram name
2. **Replace the Mermaid code** with your diagram syntax
3. **Add comments** to explain complex parts
4. **Use styling** for better visualization (optional)
5. **Save as .eraserdiagram** file
6. **Open in VS Code** with Eraser extension

## Mermaid Syntax Examples

### Flowchart
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Start] --&gt; B{Decision}
    B --&gt;|Yes| C[Action 1]
    B --&gt;|No| D[Action 2]
```

### Sequence Diagram
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Actor
    participant B as System
    A-&gt;&gt;B: Request
    B--&gt;&gt;A: Response
```

### Class Diagram
```mermaid
classDiagram
    class ClassName {
        +attribute: type
        +method()
    }
```

### ER Diagram
```mermaid
erDiagram
    ENTITY {
        int id PK
        string name
    }
```

### Gantt Chart
```mermaid
gantt
    title Project Timeline
    dateFormat YYYY-MM-DD
    section Phase 1
    Task 1 :done, task1, 2024-01-01, 2024-01-07
    Task 2 :active, task2, 2024-01-08, 2024-01-14
```
